{"id":5659,"date":"2020-08-16T08:56:00","date_gmt":"2020-08-16T12:56:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/?p=5659"},"modified":"2021-04-17T14:29:28","modified_gmt":"2021-04-17T18:29:28","slug":"st-malo-france","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/travel-log\/st-malo-france\/","title":{"rendered":"Saint-Malo, France"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Saint-Malo, known for one of the best privateers, is a small port city in Britany. With its tall city walls and its stone houses, the city really transports you to the Middle Ages.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"su-tabs su-tabs-style-default su-tabs-mobile-stack\" data-active=\"1\" data-scroll-offset=\"0\" data-anchor-in-url=\"no\"><div class=\"su-tabs-nav\"><span class=\"\" data-url=\"\" data-target=\"blank\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\">City Tour<\/span><span class=\"\" data-url=\"\" data-target=\"blank\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\">Fort Nationale<\/span><span class=\"\" data-url=\"\" data-target=\"blank\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\">Demeure de Corsaire<\/span><\/div><div class=\"su-tabs-panes\"><div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"City Tour\">\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-5677 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-5677\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200815_173119.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Walking in through the main entrance to the city, you will find the main city square. Lined with restaurants, the square is always busy with people relaxing and taking in the atmosphere.\" data-attachment-id=\"5632\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Walking in through the main entrance to the city, you will find the main city square. Lined with restaurants, the square is always busy with people relaxing and taking in the atmosphere.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200815_173119\/673604769.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Walking in through the main entrance to the city, you will find the main city square. Lined with restaurants, the square is always busy with people relaxing and taking in the atmosphere.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200815_173126.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 1] Turning back around, you will see the Castle of the Dukes of Brittany, or as it is more commonly referred to: Castle of the Duchess Anne. As you walk around the city, you will see many things referring to Duchess Anne. She was highly respected by the Bretons as she followed in her father&#039;s footsteps in attempting to maintain the region&#039;s independence. By the time of her arranged marriages to not one but two kings of France, Charles VIII and Louis XII, Brittany had lost most of its independence but it has, to this day, maintained its right to fly the Brittany flag higher than that of the French. That liberty is largely credited to Duchess Anne.\n&lt;p&gt;Built in the 15th century, the Castle today houses Town Hall and the City History Museum.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5633\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 1] Turning back around, you will see the Castle of the Dukes of Brittany, or as it is more commonly referred to: Castle of the Duchess Anne. As you walk around the city, you will see many things referring to Duchess Anne. She was highly respected by the Bretons as she followed in her father&#039;s footsteps in attempting to maintain the region&#039;s independence. By the time of her arranged marriages to not one but two kings of France, Charles VIII and Louis XII, Brittany had lost most of its independence but it has, to this day, maintained its right to fly the Brittany flag higher than that of the French. That liberty is largely credited to Duchess Anne.\n&lt;p&gt;Built in the 15th century, the Castle today houses Town Hall and the City History Museum.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200815_173126\/2458974869.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 1] Turning back around, you will see the Castle of the Dukes of Brittany, or as it is more commonly referred to: Castle of the Duchess Anne. As you walk around the city, you will see many things referring to Duchess Anne. She was highly respected by the Bretons as she followed in her father's footsteps in attempting to maintain the region's independence. By the time of her arranged marriages to not one but two kings of France, Charles VIII and Louis XII, Brittany had lost most of its independence but it has, to this day, maintained its right to fly the Brittany flag higher than that of the French. That liberty is largely credited to Duchess Anne.\n<p>Built in the 15th century, the Castle today houses Town Hall and the City History Museum.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_124214.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 2] Saint Malo is one of the few cities that remain entirely surrounded by city walls. Taking a walk on the city walls makes it easy to get a feel for the city. From the city wall near the Quic-en-Groigne Tower of the Castle offers a good view of the birthplace of Chateaubriand, a famous French writer. It is today of course a restaurant and hotel, both accessible from the main square.\" data-attachment-id=\"5664\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 2] Saint Malo is one of the few cities that remain entirely surrounded by city walls. Taking a walk on the city walls makes it easy to get a feel for the city. From the city wall near the Quic-en-Groigne Tower of the Castle offers a good view of the birthplace of Chateaubriand, a famous French writer. It is today of course a restaurant and hotel, both accessible from the main square.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_124214\/488222754.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 2] Saint Malo is one of the few cities that remain entirely surrounded by city walls. Taking a walk on the city walls makes it easy to get a feel for the city. From the city wall near the Quic-en-Groigne Tower of the Castle offers a good view of the birthplace of Chateaubriand, a famous French writer. It is today of course a restaurant and hotel, both accessible from the main square.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_104028.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"On the beach, two tidal islands are visible. There is evidence to suggest that the closer island, the &lt;i&gt;Grand B\u00e9&lt;\/i&gt; was inhabited during the Prehistoric Era. There are also remains of a chapel and of the fortifications made by Vauban. Today, it serves as the location of Chateaubriand&#039;s grave.\" data-attachment-id=\"5668\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"On the beach, two tidal islands are visible. There is evidence to suggest that the closer island, the &lt;i&gt;Grand B\u00e9&lt;\/i&gt; was inhabited during the Prehistoric Era. There are also remains of a chapel and of the fortifications made by Vauban. Today, it serves as the location of Chateaubriand&#039;s grave.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_104028\/2510592020.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">On the beach, two tidal islands are visible. There is evidence to suggest that the closer island, the <i>Grand B\u00e9<\/i> was inhabited during the Prehistoric Era. There are also remains of a chapel and of the fortifications made by Vauban. Today, it serves as the location of Chateaubriand's grave.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_104915.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 3] Chateaubriand&#039;s grave is unmarked as the author expressed his desire to rest quietly on this island after his death to listen to the sea and the wind.\" data-attachment-id=\"5669\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 3] Chateaubriand&#039;s grave is unmarked as the author expressed his desire to rest quietly on this island after his death to listen to the sea and the wind.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_104915\/2434935447.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 3] Chateaubriand's grave is unmarked as the author expressed his desire to rest quietly on this island after his death to listen to the sea and the wind.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_105329.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 4] From the Grand Be, the National Fort is visible. Built on the orders of Louis XIV and designed by Vauban, the Fort has only been taken once: by the Germans during the Second World War. The objective of the Fort was to defend against recurring attacks by the English and the British. The most famous of those attacks came in 1693 when a Dutch-Anglo fleet sent a floating mine toward the city. The ship got stuck in the rocky floor and did no harm to the city or the surrounding forts.\" data-attachment-id=\"5670\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 4] From the Grand Be, the National Fort is visible. Built on the orders of Louis XIV and designed by Vauban, the Fort has only been taken once: by the Germans during the Second World War. The objective of the Fort was to defend against recurring attacks by the English and the British. The most famous of those attacks came in 1693 when a Dutch-Anglo fleet sent a floating mine toward the city. The ship got stuck in the rocky floor and did no harm to the city or the surrounding forts.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_105329\/3682157211.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 4] From the Grand Be, the National Fort is visible. Built on the orders of Louis XIV and designed by Vauban, the Fort has only been taken once: by the Germans during the Second World War. The objective of the Fort was to defend against recurring attacks by the English and the British. The most famous of those attacks came in 1693 when a Dutch-Anglo fleet sent a floating mine toward the city. The ship got stuck in the rocky floor and did no harm to the city or the surrounding forts.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_152950.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 5] The Saint-Vincent Cathedral of Saint-Malo is a Roman Catholic Cathedral built with a mix of Roman and Gothic styles.\" data-attachment-id=\"5667\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 5] The Saint-Vincent Cathedral of Saint-Malo is a Roman Catholic Cathedral built with a mix of Roman and Gothic styles.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_152950\/1314842376.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 5] The Saint-Vincent Cathedral of Saint-Malo is a Roman Catholic Cathedral built with a mix of Roman and Gothic styles.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_150048.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The church has a Latin cross footprint with a modern Great Rose window created in 1968 featured behind the altar.\" data-attachment-id=\"5666\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The church has a Latin cross footprint with a modern Great Rose window created in 1968 featured behind the altar.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_150048\/1956825768.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The church has a Latin cross footprint with a modern Great Rose window created in 1968 featured behind the altar.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_150028.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Originally placed in the niche above one of the city wall entrances, this marble statue of the Virgin Mary dates back from the 15th century. It is referred to as the &lt;i&gt;Miraculeuse Protectrice de la Cit\u00e9 Malouine&lt;\/i&gt; (that is the &quot;Miraculous Protectress of the Malo City&quot;) due to the various legends about miracles it has performed.\" data-attachment-id=\"5665\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Originally placed in the niche above one of the city wall entrances, this marble statue of the Virgin Mary dates back from the 15th century. It is referred to as the &lt;i&gt;Miraculeuse Protectrice de la Cit\u00e9 Malouine&lt;\/i&gt; (that is the &quot;Miraculous Protectress of the Malo City&quot;) due to the various legends about miracles it has performed.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_150028\/3918816197.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Originally placed in the niche above one of the city wall entrances, this marble statue of the Virgin Mary dates back from the 15th century. It is referred to as the <i>Miraculeuse Protectrice de la Cit\u00e9 Malouine<\/i> (that is the \"Miraculous Protectress of the Malo City\") due to the various legends about miracles it has performed.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200815_174329.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 6] Famous for its apple cider and crepes, Brittany boats many Creperies specializing in these foods. Saint Malo is no exception. Enjoy a bowl of cider at one of the creperies on the way to the next destination.\" data-attachment-id=\"5634\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 6] Famous for its apple cider and crepes, Brittany boats many Creperies specializing in these foods. Saint Malo is no exception. Enjoy a bowl of cider at one of the creperies on the way to the next destination.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200815_174329\/994916949.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 6] Famous for its apple cider and crepes, Brittany boats many Creperies specializing in these foods. Saint Malo is no exception. Enjoy a bowl of cider at one of the creperies on the way to the next destination.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200816_112806-scaled.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"On the way to Stop 7, feel free to exit the city walls to get a sense of the imposing size of the city walls and the nautical feel of the city.\n&lt;p&gt;PS When you arrive at Stop 7: &lt;i&gt;Demeure de Corsaire&lt;\/i&gt;, switch over to the tab with the same name to get a closer look.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5635\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"On the way to Stop 7, feel free to exit the city walls to get a sense of the imposing size of the city walls and the nautical feel of the city.\n&lt;p&gt;PS When you arrive at Stop 7: &lt;i&gt;Demeure de Corsaire&lt;\/i&gt;, switch over to the tab with the same name to get a closer look.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200816_112806-scaled\/4106575124.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">On the way to Stop 7, feel free to exit the city walls to get a sense of the imposing size of the city walls and the nautical feel of the city.\n<p>PS When you arrive at Stop 7: <i>Demeure de Corsaire<\/i>, switch over to the tab with the same name to get a closer look.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200816_114854.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 8] A short 20-minute walk along the water leads to the town of Saint-Servan, part of the Saint Malo commune. The most famous landmark of the town is the Solidor Tower. The name comes from two Britany words: &lt;i&gt;steir&lt;\/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;dor&lt;\/i&gt; meaning the &quot;gate of the river&quot;. During its initial use in the Middle Ages, the Tower was used to control traffic and control taxes from merchants hoping to get access to the sea. It has also served as a prison and is today the Museum of the Cape Sailors.\" data-attachment-id=\"5674\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 8] A short 20-minute walk along the water leads to the town of Saint-Servan, part of the Saint Malo commune. The most famous landmark of the town is the Solidor Tower. The name comes from two Britany words: &lt;i&gt;steir&lt;\/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;dor&lt;\/i&gt; meaning the &quot;gate of the river&quot;. During its initial use in the Middle Ages, the Tower was used to control traffic and control taxes from merchants hoping to get access to the sea. It has also served as a prison and is today the Museum of the Cape Sailors.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200816_114854\/615841687.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 8] A short 20-minute walk along the water leads to the town of Saint-Servan, part of the Saint Malo commune. The most famous landmark of the town is the Solidor Tower. The name comes from two Britany words: <i>steir<\/i> and <i>dor<\/i> meaning the \"gate of the river\". During its initial use in the Middle Ages, the Tower was used to control traffic and control taxes from merchants hoping to get access to the sea. It has also served as a prison and is today the Museum of the Cape Sailors.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200816_122806.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 9] Saint-Servan is also a good place to quietly enjoy the sea breeze and taste delicious cider and seafood.\" data-attachment-id=\"5675\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 9] Saint-Servan is also a good place to quietly enjoy the sea breeze and taste delicious cider and seafood.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200816_122806\/3912635723.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 9] Saint-Servan is also a good place to quietly enjoy the sea breeze and taste delicious cider and seafood.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200816_141150.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"[Stop 10] As you take a stroll back to the old city through the park, pause to take in the nautical culture of the region.\" data-attachment-id=\"5636\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"[Stop 10] As you take a stroll back to the old city through the park, pause to take in the nautical culture of the region.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200816_141150\/3876972795.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">[Stop 10] As you take a stroll back to the old city through the park, pause to take in the nautical culture of the region.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/20200816_142542.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Overhead view of the Saint Malo old city and the surrounding ports\" data-attachment-id=\"5637\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Overhead view of the Saint Malo old city and the surrounding ports\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/02\/20200816_142542\/2019134947.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Overhead view of the Saint Malo old city and the surrounding ports<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/st_malo_map.png\" data-attachment-id=\"5697\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/st_malo_map\/3570353484.png\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><\/div>\r\n\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"Fort Nationale\">\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-5681 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-5681\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_113515-scaled.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"During times of peace, about 30 soldiers were stationed at the Fort National, with that number climbing to 100 soldiers during times of war. The cannons were mostly used to communicate with the city rather than fend off attackers.\n&lt;p&gt;The Fort is also believed to be the location of Robert Surcouf&#039;s infamous duel with 12 Prussian officers in 1871. The well-known French corsair is believed to have killed 11 Prussian officers by himself while leaving the 12th to tell the tale.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5671\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"During times of peace, about 30 soldiers were stationed at the Fort National, with that number climbing to 100 soldiers during times of war. The cannons were mostly used to communicate with the city rather than fend off attackers.\n&lt;p&gt;The Fort is also believed to be the location of Robert Surcouf&#039;s infamous duel with 12 Prussian officers in 1871. The well-known French corsair is believed to have killed 11 Prussian officers by himself while leaving the 12th to tell the tale.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_113515-scaled\/2022556862.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">During times of peace, about 30 soldiers were stationed at the Fort National, with that number climbing to 100 soldiers during times of war. The cannons were mostly used to communicate with the city rather than fend off attackers.\n<p>The Fort is also believed to be the location of Robert Surcouf's infamous duel with 12 Prussian officers in 1871. The well-known French corsair is believed to have killed 11 Prussian officers by himself while leaving the 12th to tell the tale.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_122704.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Fort was specifically designed to resist destruction. The first important design aspect is the fact that the Fort is built into the island, using the natural terrain to create a very secure base. The second design aspect is that there are no seams in the stones. The Fort was designed in a continual pattern, as evident by the floor stones, to strengthen when it gets attacked.\" data-attachment-id=\"5663\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Fort was specifically designed to resist destruction. The first important design aspect is the fact that the Fort is built into the island, using the natural terrain to create a very secure base. The second design aspect is that there are no seams in the stones. The Fort was designed in a continual pattern, as evident by the floor stones, to strengthen when it gets attacked.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_122704\/1515189987.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Fort was specifically designed to resist destruction. The first important design aspect is the fact that the Fort is built into the island, using the natural terrain to create a very secure base. The second design aspect is that there are no seams in the stones. The Fort was designed in a continual pattern, as evident by the floor stones, to strengthen when it gets attacked.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/20200815_113302.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Fort briefly served as a prison during the German occupation but has mostly served as a place for storage.\" data-attachment-id=\"5683\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Fort briefly served as a prison during the German occupation but has mostly served as a place for storage.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2021\/04\/20200815_113302\/4074394608.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Fort briefly served as a prison during the German occupation but has mostly served as a place for storage.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-typ